Title: Hold the whole census snapshot mid-sweep, not just the failure total
Created: 2026-09-06
Author: sim

--- log ---
2026-09-06T15:48Z sim created

--- body ---

## Context

Ticket 0699 (PR #387) fixed the sitter's failure accounting to derive
`state.failed` from the census each sweep, rather than accumulating it --
and added a fix ("hold the last complete census while the next one runs")
so `state.failed` doesn't blank to empty every ~30s while a re-scan is in
progress: `publish()` gates the `state.failed` recompute on
`state.scanned === state.total`.

Correctness review of PR #387 found this holds only ONE of the three terms
in the reconciliation identity (`coverage.current + state.failed + queued
=== coverage.total`). `getSDTCoverage()` reads `state.counts` live, ungated,
every `render()` call -- and `state.counts` is reset to `{}` at the top of
every sweep. So during a re-scan, `coverage.current` (and any `queued`
tally computed the same way) drops to 0 and climbs back up, WHILE
`state.failed` now sits frozen at the prior sweep's value -- a new
three-way inconsistency that did not exist before 0699 (before, all three
terms were live and reset together, so they stayed mutually consistent
even though all were momentarily wrong).

Confirmed by direct reproduction (script sampling all three terms from
inside `host.inspect()` mid-census): `identityHolds: false` for every
mid-census sample once past the first sweep, `true` only once `scanned ===
total`.

This is not a regression against anything ticket 0699 promised (its own
tests only assert the identity post-sweep, and its scope was explicitly
`state.failed`-specific) and it's an improvement over the prior
always-zeroing behavior. But it falls short of 0699's own docstring claim
("that is what makes the two numbers on screen add up") during a window
that recurs every sweep, for any library large enough that a re-scan takes
perceptible time -- the toolbar's coverage percentage will visibly flicker
downward and climb back every ~30s, while the failure banner sits frozen,
visibly disagreeing.

## Work

- Snapshot the whole census result atomically at sweep-end (current,
  failed, queued, outOfScope counts together), the way `state.pending`/
  `state.samples` are already snapshotted, rather than gating `state.failed`
  alone while `getSDTCoverage()` keeps reading live `state.counts`.
- `getSDTCoverage()` should read the held snapshot when a census is in
  progress, falling back to live counts only when idle/complete.

## Acceptance

- [ ] A test samples `coverage.current`, `state.failed`, and any `queued`
      tally simultaneously from inside a running census (not just after
      sweep() resolves) and asserts the three-way identity holds throughout,
      not only at sweep-end.
- [ ] No existing test regresses.

## Scope

Follow-up to 0699, not a blocker for it -- 0699 is a strict improvement
over the prior behavior and met its own literal acceptance criteria. This
ticket closes the gap between "add up to the correct totals" as stated and
as delivered.

